thub.com/users/angelcolorado","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angelcolorado/endurance-ui/commits/bb3a49940691caa811510e5b87c0689580262bd5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T21:36:14Z","email":"angelcolorado@outlook.com","name":"Angel Colorado"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T21:36:14Z","email":"angelcolorado@outlook.com","name":"Angel Colorado"},"message":"feat(logistics): wire event detail endpoint, promote STATUS_META to model, and add empty-state UI\n\n- EventLogisticsComponent now consumes getEventDetails() (GET /api/v1/logistics/events/:id)\n  instead of getCorrals(); state data type changed from CorralsResponse to LogisticsEventDetail\n- Header renders event name, raceDate, and lifecycle status badge from LogisticsEventDetail\n- Empty state driven by corralConfigurations.length === 0 — eliminates the removed\n  hasAnyCorrals() method that caused a post-refactor TypeError from Angular''s build cache\n- StatusMeta interface and STATUS_META constant promoted from logistics-event-list.component.ts\n  to logistics.model.ts; list component re-exports STATUS_META for spec compatibility\n- LogisticsEventDetail, EventOffering interfaces added to logistics.model.ts\n- LogisticsService.getEventDetails(): GET /api/v1/logistics/events/:id, errors propagate (no\n  catchError — 404 means the event does not exist)\n- getCorrals() URL corrected to /api/v1/logistics/events/:id/corrals; 404 still returns\n  of({ corralsByDistance: {} }) — no corrals is a valid CONFIGURATION_PHASE state\n- .angular/cache added to .gitignore\n- Specs updated: logistics.service.spec.ts (+4 getEventDetails cases), event-logistics\n  .component.spec.ts rewritten against LogisticsEventDetail contract (11 cases: header,\n  badge, cards, empty state CTA, 404→error, 500→error)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4d9da89b0efb39715720aa5a0ac4acc49ae5518","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ang