//github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/5a3a2222e896903bdd38ca3f59940538c3ca5d17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-17T16:09:41Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-17T16:09:41Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"message":"Add a detailed pattern reference and a composition guide\n\nThe per-module READMEs were thin and there was no narrative that\nexplained the building blocks in depth or showed how they assemble into\na working subsystem. Add a docs/patterns/ reference (one page per\npattern plus a primitives page) and docs/building-a-subsystem.md, all\nwritten against the module code: what each pattern builds, how events\nand data flow through it, its inputs and outputs, when to use it, and\nhow it appears in a manifest. The composition guide walks the wiring the\ncomposer derives (the shared key and its grants, hub routes, per-route\nDLQs, listener queue policies, the event-lake route, monitoring\ncoverage) through the payouts example.\n\n- New: docs/patterns/{README,primitives,event-hub,bff-service,\n  control-service,esg-service,event-lake,observability-baseline,\n  fault-monitor,regional-health-check,frontend-edge,micro-frontend}.md\n  and docs/building-a-subsystem.md.\n- Wire the new pages into the root README catalogue and Documentation\n  section and into docs/architecture/overview.md.\n- Add a \"Full documentation\" pointer from each thin module README to its\n  detailed page, and remove em dashes from the touched READMEs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2c1eb79028a478bf1b592e0f9c8284e48a60a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/trees/d2c1eb79028a478bf1b592e0f9c8284e48a60a4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/commits/5a3a2222e896903bdd38ca3f59940538c3ca5d17","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88467?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commit/5a3a2222e896903bdd38ca3f59940538c3ca5d17","node_id":"C_kwDOS26eAdoAKDVhM2EyMjIyZTg5NjkwM2JkZDM4Y2EzZjU5OTQwNTM4YzNjYTVkMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commit/a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66","sha":"a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66"}],"sha":"5a3a2222e896903bdd38ca3f59940538c3ca5d17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/5a3a2222e896903bdd38ca3f59940538c3ca5d17"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88467?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:04:13Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:04:13Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"message":"Support ingress-only ESGs (optional egress)\n\nA gateway that only receives from its external system (a payment\nprovider sending status webhooks, say) previously had to invent a fake\negress event because egress was required everywhere. Observed in the\nfirst real run of the authoring workflow, which produced an ESG that\negressed the very callback event it ingested.\n\n- esg_service: external_event_pattern is nullable; null skips the\n  whole egress path (queue, handler, rule, target, DLQs, policies, ESM)\n  and a precondition requires the webhook API instead. artefacts.egress\n  becomes optional, required only when egress is enabled.\n- schema: esgs[*].egress optional via anyOf (egress, or webhook: true).\n- composer: conditional egress artefacts, event pattern, observability\n  functions and monitored rule DLQs; manifest validation accepts\n  webhook-only ESGs and rejects ESGs with neither.\n- tests: ingress-only contract runs in esg_service (2 passing) and the\n  composer (6 passing); schema verified both directions.\n- task-builder workflow: elicitation/compose prompts now model inbound\n  callbacks through the ESG webhook (never a BFF, never fake egress),\n  and the greenfield step verifies the template scaffold exists instead\n  of silently falling back to a bare repository.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"636fdc6c8d018e696e24b36f8ad8063cafb97f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/trees/636fdc6c8d018e696e24b36f8ad8063cafb97f4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/commits/a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88467?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commit/a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66","node_id":"C_kwDOS26eAdoAKGE4NjA3MDJjYmJkMTRjOWJlNTZhMTMyNWJiZjA3NzMwODc0MjZmNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commit/a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0","sha":"a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0"}],"sha":"a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/a860702cbbd14c9be56a1325bbf0773087426f66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88467?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T22:46:09Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T22:46:09Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"message":"Add Task Builder workflow for authoring subsystems\n\nThe importable task-config YAML behind the \"Author Serverless\nSubsystem\" self-service workflow: elicit a description, compose and\nschema-validate subsystem.yaml, then land it in the app repo (creating\nit from the paved-road template if greenfield) behind a PR. Implements\nthe front-door shape described in docs/self-service-integration.md.\nPATTERN_LIBRARY_REPO and APP_TEMPLATE_REPO are left as variables here;\ninline or define them when importing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc58cc835b7743307eb66735aa68feea3d3365cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/trees/dc58cc835b7743307eb66735aa68feea3d3365cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/commits/a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88467?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commit/a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0","node_id":"C_kwDOS26eAdoAKGE5N2I1YzM0MTMyMmUyYTBkMGE4NTQ0NGQ0MjUwMzkyMmUzM2I2YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commit/64f7e641f0a340a7217fb506f81e8a8439d898a2","sha":"64f7e641f0a340a7217fb506f81e8a8439d898a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/64f7e641f0a340a7217fb506f81e8a8439d898a2"}],"sha":"a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/a97b5c341322e2a0d0a85444d42503922e33b6c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88467?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/commits/64f7e641f0a340a7217fb506f81e8a8439d898a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T22:05:37Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T22:05:37Z","email":"duvane@deslandes.co.uk","name":"dpdesi"},"message":"Rewrite self-service integration guide to be self-contained\n\nThe guide opened mid-thought, assuming the reader already knew the\nplatform-specific nouns (Task Builder, supervisor agent, AWS\nInfrastructure Flow) and the project vocabulary (manifest, composer,\nBFF, ESG). Reframe it to work for a reader landing on it cold:\n\n- Lead with the single idea (one config file drives everything) and an\n  end-to-end Mermaid diagram before any jargon, marking exactly where a\n  front door''s job stops (writes a file, opens a PR, never deploys).\n- Gloss every term on first use; ground the building blocks in a real\n  orders manifest instead of describing them abstractly.\n- Reframe the AWS Infrastructure Flow mapping as an optional retrofit\n  example, not a prerequisite.\n- Split the form/portal and chat-agent front-door shapes; keep the\n  author-subsystem vs own-connector transports, system-prompt skeleton,\n  and guardrails.\n\nFile path is unchanged, so links from the README still resolve.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7fdd0ab96b9a63d2711c827524821ef1d237b92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/trees/f7fdd0ab96b9a63d2711c827524821ef1d237b92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns/git/commits/64f7e641f0a340a7217fb506f81e8a8439d898a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88467?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dpdesi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dpdesi","id":88467,"login":"dpdesi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.