tarred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WywySenarios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WywySenarios/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WywySenarios","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WywySenarios/Wywy-Codes/commits/f49def2fa3ada3676d5cbb0685a79ad0dff8fdfd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T23:39:58Z","email":"wywyericzhu@gmail.com","name":"Eric Zhu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T23:39:58Z","email":"wywyericzhu@gmail.com","name":"Eric Zhu"},"message":"refactor(django): migrate orchestrator logging to stdlib logging\n\nReplace the custom LogWriter, _build_entry, and tail_log helper functions\nwith PipelineFileHandler, a logging.Handler that writes per-pipeline\norchestrator.log files through Python''s stdlib logging system.\n\nKey changes:\n- PipelineFileHandler — reads pipeline_id from LogRecord.extra and\n  writes JSON-lines entries to {LOG_ROOT}/{pipeline_id}/orchestrator.log\n- LEVEL_MAP — bridges legacy string-level call sites (e.g. \"WARN\") to\n  Python logging constants (logging.WARNING)\n- _write_orchestrator_log_entry — thin helper for existing positional-arg\n  callers to bridge to logger.log(level, msg, extra=...)\n- Update django LOGGING config: add pipeline_file handler and\n  orchestrator.pipeline logger, remove conditional test check for\n  RotatingFileHandler, add orchestrator_file handler for system-level\n  orchestrator events\n- Update __init__.py exports to expose new public API\n- Update test models to use EXPECTED_STAGE_NAMES constant\n- Update test_logging.py to test PipelineFileHandler emit() and\n  _write_orchestrator_log_entry via _RecordCaptureHandler","tree":{"sha":"07db502c5ea1dba9263dba850c261127e5e2d2f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WywySenarios/Wywy-Codes/git/trees/07db502c5ea1dba9263dba850c261127e5e2d2f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WywySenarios/Wywy-Codes/git/commits/f49def2f