vents","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/e99b05ccae5ffe488ab9bee88248fa0b010be821/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T14:23:57Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T14:23:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(app-studio): expose native Playwright browser tools (#585)\n\n* feat(app-studio): expose native Playwright browser tools\n\n* fix(app-studio): harden native browser sessions\n\n* fix(app-studio): close browser verification gaps\n\n* fix(app-studio): preserve browser evidence boundaries\n\n* fix(app-studio): show browser actions in threads\n\n* refactor(app-studio): use Playwright for console evidence\n\n* fix(tilt): allow preview authorization frame hop\n\n* Revert \"fix(tilt): allow preview authorization frame hop\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4abfad1b346631e78a648851c574d95d9c67f605.\n\n* fix(app-studio): keep preview tooltips above iframe","tree":{"sha":"57ebad730f1cae64ce372a0d0140c671af605506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/57ebad730f1cae64ce372a0d0140c671af605506"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/e99b05ccae5ffe488ab9bee88248fa0b010be821","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/e99b05ccae5ffe488ab9bee88248fa0b010be821","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKGU5OWIwNWNjYWU1ZmZlNDg4YWI5YmVlODgyNDhmYTBiMDEwYmU4MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1","sha":"27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1"}],"sha":"e99b05ccae5ffe488ab9bee88248fa0b010be821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/e99b05ccae5ffe488ab9bee88248fa0b010be821"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:33:08Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:33:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Generate upgrades with --reset-then-reuse-values, not --reuse-values (#587)\n\nRunning the generated upgrade command against a live BYO infrastructure\ninstall failed: chart 0.1.16 introduced the codingSandbox value block,\nand plain --reuse-values reuses the old release''s values verbatim\nwithout ever merging the new chart''s defaults — so the template crashed\non a nil .Values.codingSandbox.enabled. Any chart release that adds a\nvalue block would break every existing install the same way.\n\n--reset-then-reuse-values (Helm 3.14+) starts from the new chart''s\ndefaults and lays the operator''s previous overrides on top: new values\nappear, local edits survive.\n\nAlso make the infrastructure chart''s codingSandbox dereferences\nnil-safe, so even a hand-typed --reuse-values upgrade fails toward the\nchart default instead of a template nil-pointer error.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bbd62ad57f4260055e52eee3b5d249b529671be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/1bbd62ad57f4260055e52eee3b5d249b529671be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDI3ZDU3OWM5ZDUyMTExODAzMzVjM2I4NWFkNGYxZDVhMDI0NzcyZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7","sha":"d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7"}],"sha":"27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/27d579c9d5211180335c3b85ad4f1d5a024772e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:21:55Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:21:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump multicluster-runtime so SkipNameValidation reaches controllers (#580)\n\nThe leader-elected providers (infrastructure, code, databricks) rebuild\ntheir controller and manager on every leadership term, relying on\nmanager.Options.Controller.SkipNameValidation to allow re-registering\nthe same controller name in one process. multicluster-runtime v0.24.1\nsilently drops that option: its builder calls the unmanaged\ncontroller-runtime constructor, which never falls back to the manager''s\ncontroller config. After the first leadership term the controller fails\nto build (\"controller with name infra-instance already exists\"), the\ncallback releases the lease, and both replicas flap forever — no\nInstance created after the first lease churn is ever reconciled.\n\nUpstream fixed this on main (kubernetes-sigs/multicluster-runtime#177,\nc0b95d8: constructors now call DefaultFromConfig on the manager''s\ncontroller options) but no release contains it, so pin the current main\npseudo-version across every module that pulls multicluster-runtime.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5231c089d6b361a998d7589d935a350cc892303c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/5231c089d6b361a998d7589d935a350cc892303c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKGQ1NTU1NDcyODIwMGQ1M2RkNDUxNDdkNzc4ZDkzZTRmZTZmMGQ2ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/d4e1383c994dabee7c1656c5e78e70fb5e38f2e9","sha":"d4e1383c994dabee7c1656c5e78e70fb5e38f2e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/d4e1383c994dabee7c1656c5e78e70fb5e38f2e9"}],"sha":"d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/d55554728200d53dd45147d778d93e4fe6f0d6e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/d4e1383c994dabee7c1656c5e78e70fb5e38f2e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T05:13:43Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T05:13:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Report virtual-workspace reachability as readiness (#577)\n\n* Report virtual-workspace reachability as readiness\n\nA self-hosted provider whose APIExport virtual workspace is unreachable\nlooks entirely healthy. Templates live in the provider''s own workspace\nand are reached over the provider kubeconfig — a different URL that keeps\nworking — so the process starts, serves its API, wins leader election,\nreconciles Templates, and simply never acts on a tenant Instance.\n/healthz returned ok throughout. On a real deployment that went unnoticed\nfor days, and the eventual symptom (sandboxes stuck Pending) pointed\nnowhere near the cause.\n\nProbe the endpoint the multicluster manager actually dials: read this\nprovider''s own APIExportEndpointSlice, take the published URL, and do\ndiscovery against /clusters/*/api with the provider''s own credentials.\nProbing the address rather than inspecting the manager keeps the check\nhonest about the thing that breaks — whether THIS process can reach THAT\nURL — and does not depend on library internals, which log watch failures\nwithout surfacing them.\n\nReported on a new /readyz, and the CatalogEntry''s healthPath now points\nthere, so the hub''s BackendHealthy reflects it and the provider shows as\nnot-Ready in the portal instead of green.\n\n/healthz stays unconditional on purpose. Liveness must not fail here: the\nprovider is still serving its API and still reconciling Templates, so\ncrash-looping it would take away the work it is still doing. Readiness is\nthe right signal for \"alive but cannot do half its job\".\n\nBefore the first probe completes the provider reports ready — a process\nthat has not finished starting is not broken, and the interesting state\nis a probe that ran and failed. Recovery clears it, so a transient blip\ndoes not pin a provider unready until someone notices.\n\nThe message names the address, the underlying error, what stops working,\nand that the address comes from the platform''s shard configuration —\nbecause the person reading it is usually looking at a provider that\nappears fine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Share the virtual-workspace readiness probe across providers\n\nSix providers open an APIExport virtual workspace — app-studio, code,\ndatabricks, edges, infrastructure, kuery — and all six are self-hostable,\nso all six can be deployed somewhere that address is unreachable. The\nprobe added for infrastructure was therefore in the wrong place: one\nprovider''s private answer to a problem every provider has.\n\nMove it into provider-sdk/vwhealth, which owns the state, the probe loop\nand a /readyz handler, and convert infrastructure to it. Wire code as the\nsecond consumer, which is also what proves the package is usable from\noutside its original home rather than shaped around one caller.\n\nFour remain — app-studio, databricks, edges, kuery. They are the same\nthree edits (a Readiness value, a Watch goroutine once the signal context\nexists, a /readyz route) but each keeps its config and health wiring in a\ndifferently-shaped main, so they need doing individually rather than by\npattern-match. Wiring `code` blind produced two compile errors from\nexactly that assumption, which is the argument for not batching the rest.\n\nTests move with the package and gain coverage of the handler''s status and\nbody, plus endpoint extraction — including the empty-slice case, which is\nnormal right after install and must read as \"not yet\" rather than as a\nbad URL.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"49a121f4dd299cdea5749bf57e107f4961198def","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/49a121f4dd299cdea5749bf57e107f4961198def"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/d4e1383c994dabee7c1656c5e78e70fb5e38f2e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api