ishing flows\n\n* Polish App Studio loading and lifecycle states","tree":{"sha":"adb69a543ecbb5c1fc07718cab688e252a85d0fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/adb69a543ecbb5c1fc07718cab688e252a85d0fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/80541ae339ee76304b40efbfe9700ce03263cfbc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/80541ae339ee76304b40efbfe9700ce03263cfbc","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDgwNTQxYWUzMzllZTc2MzA0YjQwZWZiZmU5NzAwY2UwMzI2M2NmYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f","sha":"927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f"}],"sha":"80541ae339ee76304b40efbfe9700ce03263cfbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/80541ae339ee76304b40efbfe9700ce03263cfbc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T10:46:32Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T10:46:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Scale the hub to multiple replicas; fix published-app sign-in and package crawl (#510)\n\nTwo independent lines of work, both needed to run the hub as more than one pod\nand to keep published apps signing in while it rolls.\n\nHub HA (chart + hub):\n\n- replicaCount is honoured with external kcp and refused alongside embedded kcp,\n  which keeps etcd on a per-replica PVC and would otherwise give each replica\n  its own control plane.\n- Singleton controllers (provider provisioning, MCPServer, org bootstrap,\n  soft-delete) run only on the replica holding the faros-hub-controllers Lease.\n  The provider catalog controller stays exempt: it maintains the routing table\n  the request path reads, so every replica needs it.\n- Browser sessions and published-app authorization codes move to kcp-backed\n  Secrets, so a cookie or code minted by one replica resolves and revokes on all\n  of them. authorize and exchange are separate requests and a scaled hub serves\n  them from different pods.\n- Provider heartbeats are recorded on CatalogEntry.status instead of per-replica\n  memory, so liveness observed by one replica reaches the others over the\n  catalog watch.\n\ndocs/helm.md documents the two costs that scale the wrong way: the per-IP auth\nrate limiter is per replica, and embeddedGraphQL runs a schema listener per\nreplica.\n\nAccess proxy: survive a gate restart mid-sign-in\n\nAn in-flight sign-in kept its return path in a per-pod map, so any restart\nbetween the authorize redirect and the callback failed with \"invalid app access\nstate\". Flipping an app''s access mode rolls the gate deployment, which made that\nroutine. The state now travels in the browser''s return cookie (nonce, clean\npath, expiry) and is validated locally, so a callback completes against whichever\npod serves it. Nothing in the cookie is trusted: the nonce is only compared\nagainst the state parameter and the path is re-sanitised, so a tampered cookie\ncan at most produce a same-origin redirect. No signing key is involved, which\nkeeps the proxy free of credentials.\n\nSingle use is now a best-effort cache of spent nonces rather than the authority.\nLosing it costs replay detection only, because the hub''s code is itself one-use.\nThe return cookie also gains the __Host- prefix, so a sibling app under the same\npublished-apps zone cannot plant one.\n\nCallback rejections used to be one opaque 400 and exchange failures one opaque\n502, neither logged. Both now name the reason on the way out — including the\nunreachable hub URL, which is what a certificate that does not cover the gate''s\nconfigured hub address looks like from the outside. The nonce is never logged.\n\nCode provider: crawl packages every 30s\n\nAt 2m, App Studio''s publish check reported \"no component images are published\"\nfor minutes after a successful build. The cost is one host package listing per\nrepository per interval; CODE_PACKAGE_CRAWL_INTERVAL raises it for workspaces\nwith many repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d9b2afc8b4d374c086e04bf6b96e2aa32a2a4f6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/d9b2afc8b4d374c086e04bf6b96e2aa32a2a4f6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDkyN2Q3NjdmNzIyZTY5YWMwZDZmNDE2ZDU3MjJiMzJlZjc0MzMwOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7","sha":"a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7"}],"sha":"927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/927d767f722e69ac0d6f416d5722b32ef743309f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T07:54:55Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T07:54:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump providers sdk (#509)\n\n* Bump providers sdk\n\n* Quote context name in kubectl hint output\n\nCo-authored-by: mjudeikis <3225744+mjudeikis@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: mjudeikis <3225744+mjudeikis@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"820c0a3bec897b99df994e24c37711a395fa3231","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/820c0a3bec897b99df994e24c37711a395fa3231"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKGEyNjJhNmMwYWM4Yjk4YTEyZmNhMGZlYmJkNWMxNGI4OWExYjA0Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868","sha":"56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868"}],"sha":"a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/a262a6c0ac8b98a12fca0febbd5c14b89a1b04b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:35:10Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:35:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rename kedge → faros across the entire repo (#507)\n\n* Rename kedge -> faros across the entire repo\n\nThe project has always lived under the faros.sh domain while the code called\nitself kedge. This collapses the two: there is no kedge.faros.sh any more,\nonly faros.sh.\n\nMechanical, case-preserving rename with these ordered rules:\n\n  faros-kedge       -> faros           (module path)\n  kedge_faros_sh    -> faros_sh        (GraphQL-mangled group identifiers)\n  KedgeFarosSh      -> FarosSh         (GraphQL type prefixes)\n  kedge.faros.sh    -> faros.sh        (API groups; before the generic rule)\n  KEDGE/Kedge/kedge -> FAROS/Faros/faros\n\nWhat that covers:\n  - module github.com/faroshq/faros-kedge -> github.com/faroshq/faros\n  - API groups *.kedge.faros.sh -> *.faros.sh; the root group is now faros.sh\n  - env vars KEDGE_* -> FAROS_* (hard cut, no compatibility aliases)\n  - HTTP headers X-Kedge-* -> X-Faros-*\n  - template tokens ${kedge.devImage.*} -> ${faros.*}, kedgeMode -> farosMode\n  - images ghcr.io/faroshq/kedge-* -> faros-*; charts faros-hub / faros-agent\n  - dirs apis/kedge, cmd/kedge{,-hub,-release}, deploy/charts/kedge-*\n  - generated CRDs/APIExports/APIResourceSchemas renamed in content and filename\n    (text-renamed, not regenerated)\n\nmarkEdgeConnected/markEdgeDisconnected are mark+Edge, not kedge, and are\ndeliberately left alone.\n\nThree changes are NOT a plain text substitution, because a substitution alone\nwould have been wrong:\n\n  - .github/workflows/images.yaml derived the hub and agent image names from\n    ${{ github.repository }}, which would have kept publishing kedge-hub and\n    kedge-agent while every chart pulls faros-hub/faros-agent. They are now\n    spelled out as repository_owner + a literal name, matching helm-images.yaml\n    and the provider matrix.\n  - The application/simple-webapp templates embed the Vite dev shim as a base64\n    payload, which a text pass cannot see into. It still imported\n    file:///kedge/bin/preview-console-plugin.mjs while the dev overlay now\n    mounts /faros/bin. Both payloads were decoded, renamed and re-encoded.\n  - The databricks assistant skill artifact records a content digest over the\n    skill text. Renaming the text changed the digest, so manifest.yaml and the\n    chart catalogentry now carry the recomputed value.\n\nVerified: go vet and go test (excluding cluster-backed e2e) are clean across all\neleven modules plus the linux-only dev-agent. Every changed file other than the\nthree cases above was re-derived from its parent revision by reapplying the\nrules and byte-compared, so the rest of the diff is provably the rename and\nnothing else.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* templates: pin scaffolds to v0.1.3\n\nfaros-scaffold-application and faros-scaffold-simple-webapp were renamed from\nkedge-scaffold-* and re-tagged v0.1.3 with the same rename applied inside.\n\nThe published image path follows GITHUB_REPOSITORY, so the repo rename moved\npublishing to ghcr.io/faroshq/faros-scaffold-*. The v0.1.2 tag only ever\nexisted under the old kedge-scaffold-* package names, so the renamed template\nreferences would have 404''d until this bump — nothing re-publishes an old tag\nunder a new package name.\n\nBumps together, as the templates require: the scaffold git refs and the\nsampleValues/default image tags.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix two rename fallouts caught by CI: escaped-regex group and gofmt\n\nNeither was visible to the text substitution or to go vet/go test locally.\n\n1. The Template instanceCRD.group validator is a regex with ESCAPED dots:\n\n     ^infrastructure\\.kedge\\.faros\\.sh$\n\n   The `kedge.faros.sh -> faros.sh` rule matches the literal group string, so\n   it never fired on the escaped form; the generic `kedge -> faros` rule then\n   produced `^infrastructure\\.faros\\.faros\\.sh$`. Every Template was rejected\n   at admission, which is why the infraprovider e2e suite could not seed its\n   catalog. Fixed in the kubebuilder marker and both generated CRD copies.\n\n   Swept for the same failure in every other encoding (\\. . - _ and\n   concatenated): the only other hits are `faros-faros-hub`, which is helm''s\n   <release>-<chart> naming and was `kedge-kedge-hub` before — correct as is.\n\n2. Shortening the group strings changed the width of aligned trailing\n   comments, so gofmt reformatted 15 files. Alignment only, no code change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* providers: build against the in-tree provider-sdk\n\nThe providers require published provider-sdk versions (v0.0.1/v0.0.8/v0.0.13)\nwith no replace, so only go.work made them compile against this repo''s copy.\nCI has no go.work, so it silently linked the PUBLISHED SDK instead — which is\nstill pre-rename and writes ClusterRole \"kedge:providers:bind:<export>\". The\nprovider e2e suite asserts the renamed \"faros:providers:bind:<export>\" and\nfailed on exactly that, reproducibly in CI and never locally.\n\nsplit-provider-sdk.yaml''s own header already describes this arrangement —\n\"providers depend on this SDK via replace => ../../provider-sdk in the\nmonorepo\" — it had just never been applied. Adding it makes CI match local and\nkeeps the SDK in lockstep with the rename instead of straddling a published\nboundary mid-rename.\n\ngo mod tidy on agents, app-studio, infrastructure, kuery and vibe-studio: the\nin-tree SDK''s dependency set differs from the v0.0.1 they had pinned.\n\nVerified the way CI builds (GOWORK=off): all nine providers compile, and the\nquickstart binary now carries only \"faros:providers:bind:\" — no kedge string\nsurvives in the linked SDK.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* e2e: run provider suites against the in-tree provider-sdk\n\nReverts the per-provider `replace => ../../provider-sdk` added in b03a416b and\nfixes the underlying problem in CI instead.\n\nThe replace was wrong. go.work.template and hack/provider-sdk-cutover.sh both\nrecord that those replaces were deliberately DROPPED once the SDK was\npublished, and each provider Dockerfile says so too (\"uses the published\nfaros-provider-sdk (no replace), fetched from the proxy\"). Provider images\nbuild with the provider directory as the Docker context, so ../../provider-sdk\nis outside the context and every provider image build failed with\n\"reading /provider-sdk/go.mod: no such file or directory\".\n\nThe real issue is narrower: the provider e2e suites build provider binaries and\nassert on their behaviour, so they must exercise THIS commit''s SDK. Workspace\nmode is how the monorepo develops the SDK and its consumers together, but\ngo.work is gitignored, so CI never had one and silently linked the published\nSDK — which is pre-rename and writes \"kedge:providers:bind:<export>\" while the\nsuite asserts the renamed \"faros:providers:bind:<export>\". That is why it failed\nonly in CI and never locally.\n\nThe e2e job now builds the workspace before running, leaving go.mod, the\npublished-module contract and the image builds untouched.\n\nNote for after merge: provider IMAGES still link the last published provider-sdk\n(v0.0.1/v0.0.8/v0.0.13), so they keep writing kedge-prefixed bind ClusterRoles\nuntil provider-sdk is re-tagged from this branch and each provider''s require is\nbumped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68722137b3f5c10f80d203614d2f2c2e0ba5b0b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/68722137b3f5c10f80d203614d2f2c2e0ba5b0b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDU2YjJlMTIzYTc4NmNiNDFjOGQxMmY3YzJkNTI1ZTgzZTMxNWM4Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea","sha":"18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea"}],"sha":"56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/56b2e123a786cb41c8d12f7c2d525e83e315c868"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5685031?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:27:31Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:27:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add App Studio publishing and gated app access (#506)\n\n* Rework app publishing\n\n* wire in proxy image CI\n\n* fix tilt\n\n* fix lint & app studio\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt>","tree":{"sha":"c7b8d55cdf0013b9c2fc0a82f04bddeaad905838","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/c7b8d55cdf0013b9c2fc0a82f04bddeaad905838"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDE4MzI2MzkwMTM4ZDU4N2YxNDhmZTNiMzJlZmE3MWI5NTk1ODlmZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584","sha":"002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584"}],"sha":"18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/18326390138d587f148fe3b32efa71b959589fea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5685031?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T23:29:50Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T23:29:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add Provider Actions and Databricks-backed App Studio integrations (#499)\n\n* Improve App Studio execution and verification flows\n\n* Improve application studio execution and UI flows\n\n* Improve application studio workflow and runtime state handling\n\n* Harden App Studio provider action recovery\n\n* move provider actions to virtual-workspace\n\n* remove committed kind kubeconfig and ignore stray root-level dumps\n\nThe extension-less file ''tilt'' was a kind-cluster kubeconfig carrying a\nclient private key; *.kubeconfig was already ignored but nothing caught\nfiles without the extension.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* rework menu & few fixes\n\n* Centralize Provider Actions runtime binding overlays\n\n* Relax App Studio no-progress termination\n\n* Preserve read evidence during App Studio context reduction\n\n* port browser to infra\n\n* clean old browser workers\n\n* Stabilize App Studio integration runtime\n\n* Fix dev-agent image build context\n\n* Improve App Studio project creation flow and preview diagnostics\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43e0976e3110eae8f48df0c0446ffa11bb42fbfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/43e0976e3110eae8f48df0c0446ffa11bb42fbfa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDAwMjcxNzM3MWExZTMxMWZhZGQwODExMjk4ODY5MTBhNzNlMWI1ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6","sha":"5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6"}],"sha":"002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/002717371a1e311fadd081129886910a73e1b584"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T06:55:01Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T06:55:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"app-studio: vibe-studio engine retrofit + creation wizard, code explorer, edit-reliability fixes (#500)\n\n* Retrofit vibe to app\n\n* app-studio: vibe-studio engine retrofit + creation wizard, code explorer, edit-reliability fixes\n\nApp Studio now runs the vibe-studio engine model end to end:\n\nReconcilers & permissions\n- Multicluster APIExport Project reconciler lifecycles instances from self-contained\n  bindings; Session CR (Postgres projection + purge finalizer) and Studio singleton\n  (shared searxng web search) reconcilers; per-project ServiceAccount identity.\n- Handlers inverted to spec-only writes; instances/repos/commits converge in-loop.\n- Permission claims: infra instances + repositories + searxngs + serviceaccounts/\n  secrets/RBAC, with infra/code identity hashes (init_cmd + manifest + catalogentry\n  + chart + Makefile auto-discovery).\n\nScaffolding & wizard-first creation\n- Templates'' spec.development.scaffold seeds the workspace at template bind (repo =\n  scaffold); tracked as uncommitted so commit convergence + dev-sync pick it up.\n- Blueprint-first creation: /api/projects/plan + SSE /api/projects/stream surface\n  live steps (\"Attaching scaffold to <template>\"); NewProjectWizard is the default\n  landing flow.\n- Code workbench tab: read-only explorer of the live dev workspace\n  (/files + /files/content + CodeExplorer.vue).\n\nEdit-reliability fixes (root-caused via run-event forensics)\n- Mutation gate uses the recorded complete-read version instead of the model''s\n  fabricated token; read limit is clamped, not rejected.\n- Context reduction no longer leaves empty tool-call objects the model imitated.\n- Commit convergence no longer aborted by transient instance update conflicts.\n- Promote guard refuses while the workspace is dirty.\n\nAlso carries shared portalkit (toast) + design-system updates across providers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* app-studio: meaningful auto-commit messages from the reconciler\n\nThe commit-convergence loop wrote \"chore: sync workspace (N files)\", which\nsays nothing about the change. Build the message from the actual paths:\nsubject names the file for a single change, or the count + top-level areas\n(e.g. \"Update 3 files, delete 1 file in web, api\") for many; the body lists\nthe paths. Deterministic, no coupling to the assistant layer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"111a3014201e151f718515fec074b101e2622a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/111a3014201e151f718515fec074b101e2622a3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDVlN2EyZDYyMjRiYjIxMWE0ZTU4N2VkMjQ3MjJhOTBhMWUxYjZhZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163","sha":"0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163"}],"sha":"5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/5e7a2d6224bb211a4e587ed24722a90a1e1b6af6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:20:21Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:20:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Vibe-Studio (#491)\n\n* Vibe-Studio\n\n* feat(vibe-studio): commit workspace to git from the reconciler\n\nStudio edits reached the sandbox but never git, so a project''s repository\nheld only the seed commit. Git now converges on the Session reconcile loop\nin the usual desired-vs-observed shape: the store keeps a monotonic\nworkspace revision, the Session records the revision it last pushed, and\nthey are reconciled into a commit. No write-path hook — a burst of edits\nduring one turn collapses into a single commit, and a failed push simply\nretries next pass.\n\nCommits wait for the turn to finish, and describe the actual change: the\nrequest that drove it as the subject, the files it touched as the body,\nread from the events since the last commit (the folded state cannot supply\nthis — pending input is consumed the moment a turn starts, which is why\nevery commit read \"sync workspace\").\n\nAlso in this change:\n\n- Instance values are filtered by declared TYPE, not just name. The model\n  proposed `expose: true` for an object-typed input; the API server\n  rejected the whole instance and the controller retried it forever. The\n  intake catalog now lists inputs with their types, and an Invalid error\n  is recorded on the binding instead of retried, since only a spec change\n  can fix it.\n- Restore the scaffold pins on the application and simple-webapp\n  templates. Without spec.development.scaffold, provisioning takes the\n  \"nothing to seed\" path and every new project gets an EMPTY sandbox.\n- Portal: stop the conversation jumping while events stream in. Rebuilding\n  innerHTML resets scrollTop, and assigning it under scroll-behavior:\n  smooth animated the correction at 400ms intervals. Position is restored\n  exactly, smooth scrolling is gone, and renders are deferred entirely\n  while the user is scrolling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vibe-studio): promote to production as a spec write\n\nProduction is a second environment on the Project, not a separate\npipeline: promote appends `spec.environments[production]` with the same\ntemplate in kedgeMode: production and the images pinned into the inputs\nthe template declares, and the existing Project reconciler converges the\ninstance exactly as it does the development sandbox. Re-promoting a\nnewer image replaces the environment in place; the sandbox keeps running\nthroughout.\n\nThe development contract on the Project spec now records\n`components[].imageInput`, copied from the Template at approve time, so\npromotion stays template-agnostic without any reconciler reading\nTemplates. Projects created before this get the contract backfilled from\ntheir Template on first promote.\n\nTwo guards, both deliberate:\n\n- Digest tether: promotion refuses while the workspace has uncommitted\n  changes, or when nothing has been committed at all. The promoted\n  environment records the commit in spec/status `revision`, so what is\n  running is always traceable to a tree — the app-studio bug this\n  provider set out not to inherit.\n- No partial ships: a component with an imageInput and no image fails the\n  whole promotion, naming the component, rather than deploying half an\n  app on scaffold defaults.\n\nThe Session reconciler mirrors the production environment''s status into\nthe `production` checkpoint (\"live on 2613af6 — https://…\"), and the\nportal grows a ship panel on the Status tab.\n\nVerified end to end against the dev hub: the production instance reached\nReady on its own address with its own database, running the pinned\nimages while the dev sandbox continued on the platform dev image.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vibe-studio): seed the scaffold''s build workflow instead of dropping it\n\nEvery scaffold ships .github/workflows/build.yaml — smoke test, then one\nRailpack image per component pushed to ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>/<component>\ntagged sha-<commit>, with component names matching the template''s. The\nscaffold fetch was filtering `.github/` out, so seeded projects arrived\nwith no CI at all: no builds on commit, and nothing for promotion to pin\na digest to.\n\nKeeping it means the pipeline comes with the scaffold and the commit\nreconciler''s pushes to the default branch trigger it, so no build-config\ngenerator is needed at all.\n\nCommitting under .github/workflows/ requires the `workflow` OAuth scope\non the Code connection; without it the host rejects the whole commit, not\njust that file. The git checkpoint now says so, and says to reconnect\ngranting the scope, rather than passing GitHub''s wording straight\nthrough.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(infrastructure): pin templates to scaffold v0.1.2\n\nThe v0.1.1 scaffolds'' smoke tests asserted their own placeholder content\n(\"kedge\" on the page, the demo /api/messages round-trip), so CI went red\non a project''s first real change. v0.1.2 probes structurally instead —\nthe tier must boot and serve a 2xx, plus /api/health, which AGENTS.md\ndeclares a contract every project keeps.\n\nBumps both scaffold refs and the application template''s image defaults\nand sampleValues, which are pinned to the same tag by convention. The\nv0.1.2 images are published for web, api, and app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vibe-studio): render the ship panel for pre-imageInput projects\n\nThe development contract was backfilled from the Template only when\npromoting. A project created before image inputs were recorded therefore\nshowed an empty ship panel with the button disabled, which reads as\n\"this template has nothing to build\" rather than \"we did not record\nwhere its images go\". Backfill on the read path too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vibe-studio): start building as soon as the sandbox is up\n\nA new project landed in studio idle: the preview served the scaffold''s\nhello-world until the user typed something like \"build it\". The wizard\nhad already asked what to build and the user had already approved the\nanswer, so that asked for the same decision twice.\n\nProvision completion now also emits the opening instruction — title,\nsummary, success criteria, and \"edit the scaffold rather than\nre-bootstrapping\" — as a user message. NextAction therefore returns\nrun-studio-turn and the existing turn machinery picks it up; emitting an\nevent instead of special-casing the engine keeps the kickoff in the\ntranscript and replayable like any other turn.\n\nProvisioning finishes in the reconciler but only the API process runs the\nengine, so the session view now kicks owed turns (single-flighted, and\nadvance() already CASes on turn.started). A crashed replica leaving input\npending recovers the same way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vibe-studio): give every project web search and page fetch\n\nThe assistant could not look anything up: asked to check what a product\ndoes from its GitHub page, it answered \"I can''t access GitHub from\nhere\" and told the user to paste the README — the exact errand the\nwizard exists to remove.\n\nSearch rides the binding contract rather than a new subsystem. Approval\nnow writes a second binding, `search`, pointing at a searxng instance\n(the infrastructure template: a private SearXNG with the JSON API on, no\npublic URL, no credential — kcp RBAC on the instance is the gate), and\nthe Project reconciler creates it, mirrors its status, and deletes it\nwith the project exactly as it does the sandbox. Every project gets one;\nthere is nothing to configure, unlike the agents provider where a\nwebsearch Connection is opt-in.\n\nBecause a project now binds more than one instance, provisioning and\npromotion address the runtime by binding name instead of taking the\nfirst infrastructure binding they see.\n\nweb_fetch needs no backend and is guarded the way the agents provider\nguards it: the dial control checks the RESOLVED address, so a URL the\nmodel chose can never reach loopback, private, or link-local space. A\nprompt injection must not turn the studio into a network probe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vibe-studio): claim searxngs in the CatalogEntry, not just the APIExport\n\nThe search binding was written onto every new Project and then nothing\nhappened: the Project reconciler could not create the instance, so the\nwhole reconcile errored and the project never got a status at all.\n\nPermission claims live in three places, and init_cmd.go is only one of\nthem. The APIExport declares what the provider MAY claim; the tenant\nAPIBinding decides what it DOES claim, and the hub writes that from the\nCatalogEntry (manifest.yaml for dev registration, the chart template for\nprod) at Enable time. A claim missing there is invisible until a\nreconciler is denied.\n\nNote for existing tenants: the hub only rewrites claims on Enable, so an\nalready-enabled workspace keeps its old set until re-enabled (or its\nAPIBinding is patched).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vibe-studio): attribute each instance to its own template\n\nA project''s search backend was labelled kedge.faros.sh/template:\napplication — the app''s template — because DesiredInstance took the\nlabel from the Project. A project binds instances of several templates\nnow, so the infrastructure provider listed a searxng instance as if it\nwere a web application.\n\nAttribution moves to the binding, which is where it belongs: the\napprove path stamps the app template on the runtime binding and searxng\non the search binding, promotion inherits the runtime''s, and the\nreconciler labels each instance from its own ref. Bindings written\nbefore the field existed fall back to the Project''s template, so nothing\nin flight changes meaning.\n\nProjects schema v260801-005 (kcp prunes fields the schema does not\ndeclare).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vibe-studio): leave an instance unlabelled rather than guess its template\n\nThe fallback for bindings written before the template field existed\napplied the Project''s template to every binding, which is how a searxng\ninstance came to be filed as an \"application\" in the first place. Only\nthe runtime binding is known to come from the Project''s template; for\nanything else, no attribution beats wrong attribution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vibe-studio): one shared search backend per workspace, not per project\n\nEvery project provisioning its own SearXNG ran N identical pods to\nanswer the same questions: a search index has no per-project state, so\nthe instance belongs to the workspace.\n\nAdds Studio, the workspace''s vibe-studio installation: a cluster-scoped\nsingleton (studios/default, like mcpservers/default) holding the\nservices every project shares and the settings that apply across them.\nSearch is its first field; a shared browser instance or a workspace-wide\ndefault model are fields, not new CRDs.\n\nThe API writes the singleton on a workspace''s first authenticated\nrequest after enabling the provider — reconcilers converge objects, they\ndo not invent them, and resolving the searxng Template needs the\ncaller''s identity — so search is warm before the first project exists.\nThe Studio reconciler then owns the instance: create, status mirror, and\nteardown via finalizer when the Studio is deleted or search disabled.\nProjects no longer carry a search binding, and the studio turn resolves\nthe backend from Studio.status.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vibe-studio): fill the ship panel from the images CI actually built\n\nPromotion asked the user to paste an image reference, while the code\nprovider already knew the answer: the scaffold''s workflow publishes one\nimage per component tagged sha-<commit>, and the PackageController\ncrawls the registry into Package records.\n\nThe ship panel now resolves each component''s digest by matching\nsha-<committedRevision> against those packages, and promote fills in\nwhatever the caller leaves out — so shipping is a button. Matching is on\nthe exact tag: sha-<commit>-linux-arm64 is a per-arch manifest, and\npromoting it would pin production to one architecture.\n\nResolving BY COMMIT is what makes the digest tether exact rather than\napproximate. If CI has not published for the commit in git, the panel\nsays so and the button stays disabled, instead of quietly offering an\nolder image as though it were this tree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vibe-studio): mint the registry pull credential for production\n\nProduction runs the private images the project''s own CI published, so a\nfresh production deployment sat in ErrImagePull with nothing to fix it.\n\nThe credential is the git-host token the project already has — on GitHub\nthe token that pushed the image can pull it — and the convention is the\ninfrastructure provider''s, which bridges a tenant Secret named\n\"<instance>-registry\" into the runtime namespace and attaches it to\nthat namespace''s default ServiceAccount. That bridge is generic, not\napp-studio''s: minting the Secret is all vibe-studio owes it.\n\nDone in the Project reconciler rather than at promote time, so a rotated\ntoken reaches production without anyone re-promoting. It needs no claim\non Connections: the API resolves where the token lives as the CALLER and\nrecords it on spec.repository.tokenSecret, the same self-contained-spec\ncontract the instance bindings use, and the reconciler reads the Secret\nwith the claim it already has. Existing projects get the reference\nbackfilled on their next promote.\n\nThe registry host is read from the promoted image rather than assumed,\nso a project published somewhere other than ghcr gets a credential for\nthe right host.\n\nProjects schema v260801-006.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vibe-studio): mint the pull credential before creating instances\n\nThe infrastructure provider bridges the registry Secret into the runtime\nnamespace while reconciling the INSTANCE, so a credential written after\nthe instance was created is not picked up until something else touches\nit — a fresh promotion would sit in ImagePullBackOff even though the\nSecret existed.\n\nMinting now happens before the instance loop, so the first reconcile of\na new production instance already finds it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* agents rework and vibe vibing\n\n* Agents deep deep\n\n* go mod tidy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"06e7e1ab21bf13ffd6c52e050691dea13244f515","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/trees/06e7e1ab21bf13ffd6c52e050691dea13244f515"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/git/commits/0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qZj9oAKDA2NjJhNjJkNzQ1ODQ4MmMwYjM1YzU4Yjg5OWQ1ZDk5MDk1ZDUxNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commit/a3ea4185b9e5f5b330f13cc8c180d73a7f44e542","sha":"a3ea4185b9e5f5b330f13cc8c180d73a7f44e542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/a3ea4185b9e5f5b330f13cc8c180d73a7f44e542"}],"sha":"0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits/0662a62d7458482c0b35c58b899d5d99095d5163"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-infrastructure/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=1a44be178b05010c74732b8f726d84451acb26dc&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A00%3A41.624Z"}');
INSERT INTO collection_pages VALUES('7920415bc8bd61806f9781c846ea36de56cb5576763e90620f9b516437873629','335c6bb70daeca92fcfa9f5a46dd5bf112b74d0f9c0524ba60b6a468d556f1d4','{"hasNext":true,"items":[{"author":{"account":{"login":"cwilhit","providerType":"User"},"email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T12:30:31Z","committedDate":"2026-10-08T12:30:31Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"7755987f620b8d7873fe9f1ae9d2bf9d1d2b2764"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"cwilhit","providerType":"User"},"email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T01:53:19Z","committedDate":"2026-10-08T01:53:19Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"6ebdc11fca7122038a0e1bccd26b7a9943f1b91f"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"cwilhit","providerType":"User"},"email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T01:24:04Z","committedDate":"2026-10-08T01:24:04Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"48862274e0a476732dd3a71f78f5c7ce3b4c5822"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"cwilhit","providerType":"User"},"email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T23:24:23Z","committedDate":"2026-10-07T23:24:23Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"741e6ef9f1344388c9a2303a9ec7b874e1924df1"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"cwilhit","providerType":"User"},"email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T07:57:59Z","committedDate":"2026-10-07T07:57:59Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"35882b57162a4c0a576d2df8b8d90642b28c9bde"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"mjudeikis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-06T18:17:58Z","committedDate":"2026-10-06T18:17:58Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"de8eaea358538c1fb3ffdc20b691ed048827acf9"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"cwilhit","providerType":"User"},"email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-05T22:02:49Z","committedDate":"2026-10-05T22:02:49Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"1a5a68a6ed7404b894e03b0e0670585f4c43d5df"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"mjudeikis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-04T15:51:43Z","committedDate":"2026-10-04T15:51:43Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266326222,"sha":"bcf97b740c08cd8ed4192def88c11b0a9070346c"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"mjudeikis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-03T05:38:02Z","committedDate":"2026-10-03T05:38:02Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:24:07.454Z","repositoryId":1266