"followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/96fde58bfe5767f3a28be127194f36c3e905a2df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:24:36Z","email":"cdwilhite0601@gmail.com","name":"Craig D Wilhite"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:24:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(code): share GitHub package discovery and honor rate limits (#675)\n\n* fix(code): share GitHub package discovery and honor rate limits\n\n* fix(code): use native controller retries for package polling\n\n* Fix package dependency wakeups and paginated request fairness\n\n* Bound GitHub request state admission per tenant\n\n* Simplify GitHub polling by removing tenant admission policy","tree":{"sha":"7c6a512608037b42a4bd909f544da182c3585fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/trees/7c6a512608037b42a4bd909f544da182c3585fd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/commits/96fde58bfe5767f3a28be127194f36c3e905a2df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/96fde58bfe5767f3a28be127194f36c3e905a2df","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qaztoAKDk2ZmRlNThiZmU1NzY3ZjNhMjhiZTEyNzE5NGYzNmMzZTkwNWEyZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da","sha":"9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da"}],"sha":"96fde58bfe5767f3a28be127194f36c3e905a2df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/96fde58bfe5767f3a28be127194f36c3e905a2df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T13:30:24Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T13:30:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: one front door — README, docs landing and getting-started describe the product that ships (#665)\n\n* docs: one front door — README, docs landing and getting-started describe the product that ships\n\nThe README, the docs index and the CLI each told a different story: the\nREADME and docs still described the previous product (reverse tunnels for\nhome labs, Site/VirtualWorkload/Placement resources, a hosted hub at\nconsole.faros.sh that does not resolve), while the tree ships a kcp-based\ncontrol plane with providers, actions, per-workspace MCP and edges.\n\n- README: what faros is, honest alpha status, the providers in the tree,\n  install via the OCI chart, a quickstart that matches the CLI, the\n  security posture and where the hardening values live, an accurate CLI\n  reference, and the relationship to kcp and Platform Mesh in one paragraph.\n- docs/index.md and _config.yml: same story; the dead resource table and\n  the home-lab framing are gone; the documentation table lists the pages\n  that exist.\n- docs/getting-started.md: rebuilt around `faros dev init`, mirroring the\n  steps the command prints (faros.localhost, dev-token, edge kubeconfig\n  secret, hub NodePort on the Docker network) instead of make targets and\n  resources that no longer exist.\n- CLI: `faros login` no longer defaults to a hosted hub that does not\n  exist; it takes --hub-url or FAROS_HUB_URL and fails with a clear\n  message otherwise. The root command''s tagline matches the README.\n- Small wording fixes: security.md, the hub chart README, the code\n  provider README''s example hostname, CONTRIBUTING''s Go version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: keep kcp under the hood\n\nkcp is how workspaces are served, not what faros is. The README, docs\nlanding page, chart README and CLI tagline now describe the product\nwithout it; one \"Under the hood\" paragraph says what it is and who\nmeets it (operators and provider authors, not users).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: no faros-agent binary; the guide uses the per-cluster kubeconfigs dev init writes\n\nReview follow-ups: cmd/ holds faros, faros-hub, graphql and release, and\nthe agent is ''faros agent''; the guide exports the hub kubeconfig before\nreading the edge secret and addresses the worker cluster through its own\nkubeconfig file, which is what ''faros dev init'' prints.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a4a194261081f7ddf4e788f4808736df77d37482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/trees/a4a194261081f7ddf4e788f4808736df77d37482"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/commits/9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qaztoAKDk3MThlMGVlYzk1NjU5MTI1YzUxNjdlNzM5NDcyMDYyYmZkMjU1ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542","sha":"acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542"}],"sha":"9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/9718e0eec95659125c5167e739472062bfd255da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:38:59Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:38:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(portal): stop handing provider bundles the raw id token and pin bundles with SRI (#637)\n\n* fix(portal): stop handing provider bundles the raw id token and pin bundles with SRI\n\nProvider micro-frontends are classic scripts the portal injects into its\nown document, so a bundle executes as fully trusted code. Three things\nmade that worse than necessary (security remediation plan 3.1):\n\n- ProviderFrame.vue and DashboardTile.vue handed every bundle\n  farosContext.token, the user''s raw OIDC id token, which provider\n  portals then placed in Authorization themselves. Any bundle could\n  exfiltrate it or call any hub endpoint as the user.\n- The bundle was loaded with no integrity attribute, so a main.js\n  swapped behind spec.ui.url after registration ran unchanged.\n- The portal CSP allowed ''unsafe-inline'' scripts.\n\nHost fetch: the host now places a host-owned fetch on farosContext\n(portal/src/providers/providerFetch.ts) that resolves relative URLs\nagainst the portal origin, injects Authorization and the X-Faros-*\ntenant headers from host state, and refuses everything outside the\nprovider''s allow list (/services/providers/<name>/,\n/ui/providers/<name>/, /graphql/, /clusters/, /api/orgs/<org>/, and\nGET /api/providers). token stays for one release as a deprecated getter\nthat warns once per provider. portalkit/tenant.ts gains\nproviderFetch(ctx) (prefers ctx.fetch, falls back to fetch + ctx.token\non an older host); copies are synced and every in-repo provider portal\nroutes its hub requests through it.\n\nSRI: the catalog reconciler hashes <spec.ui.url>/main.js (or a\nbuiltin''s embedded main.js) and records sha384 in\nCatalogEntry.status.ui.mainJSIntegrity and on the registry record,\nkeyed on status.reportedVersion (falling back to spec.version) so a\nheartbeat reporting a new version re-hashes, with a 10-minute resync\notherwise. /api/providers exposes mainJSIntegrity; the loader sets\nintegrity + crossorigin=\"anonymous\" and warns when no pin exists.\nOrg-owned providers travel the edge tunnel and stay unpinned.\n\nCSP: script-src ''self'' with no ''unsafe-inline''. The theme pre-paint\nbootstrap moves from an inline script in index.html to\nportal/public/theme-bootstrap.js; the built index.html has no inline\nscript. docs/providers.md and AGENTS.md now describe the custom-element\nmodel, the host fetch, SRI, the trust statement, and the sandboxed\niframe follow-up instead of the stale iframe/postMessage design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(portal): load the pinned provider bundle without crossorigin\n\nThe bundle is fetched from /ui/providers/<name>/main.js, a same-origin path\nthe portal builds itself. A same-origin response has type \"basic\", which the\nbrowser integrity-checks on its own, so SRI does not need the crossorigin\nattribute here.\n\nSetting it was not merely redundant. crossorigin makes the load a CORS-mode\nrequest, and the hub''s UI proxy negotiates no CORS at all: it serves the\nbundle same-origin from the embedded FS or the provider upstream and never\nsets Access-Control-Allow-Origin. Keeping the attribute risked breaking every\nprovider UI for no benefit.\n\nThe old comment claimed crossorigin was required to enforce integrity even\nsame-origin, which is not what the spec says, and asserted ''anonymous'' sends\nno credentials — also wrong, since ''anonymous'' maps to credentials mode\n\"same-origin\". Replace it with the actual reasoning.\n\nAdd a Go test locking in the server-side premise: the UI proxy answers a\nbundle request carrying an Origin header with no CORS headers, so a future\nchange that starts negotiating CORS has to revisit the loader deliberately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hub): decide the UI pin error path on the current cache entry\n\npinUIIntegrity snapshots the cache entry under the mutex, drops the lock to\nfetch and hash the bundle over the network, then re-locks on the error path.\nIt still decided on the pre-fetch snapshot: when the snapshot''s version\ndiffered from the version being pinned it unconditionally deleted the entry.\n\nA hash fetch is a bounded-but-slow network round trip, and reconciles for one\nprovider are not serialised. A concurrent reconcile that pinned a newer\nversion while the fetch was in flight had its record deleted by the slower\ngoroutine''s failure, unpinning a bundle that was in fact successfully pinned\nuntil some later reconcile re-hashed it.\n\nRe-read the entry under the lock and decide on that. An entry that changed\nsince the snapshot belongs to another reconcile and is left alone; only an\nuntouched pin for a superseded version is still dropped, preserving the\ndocumented behaviour that the portal loads the new bundle unpinned rather\nthan with a hash that cannot match it.\n\nThe regression test forces the interleaving with a client that blocks until\nthe test has performed the concurrent write, so it fails deterministically\nagainst the old code rather than depending on timing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(apis): correct what a nil CatalogEntryStatus.UI means\n\nThe field was documented as nil only when the hub serves no /main.js for the\nentry. The controller in fact sets status.ui only when it holds a pin\n(prov.MainJSIntegrity != \"\"), so a served bundle that is merely unpinned\nright now — a transient hash fetch failure, a version change whose re-hash\nhas not landed, or a hub too old to compute pins — also yields nil.\n\nA client reading nil as \"this provider has no UI\" would therefore be wrong\nfor exactly the cases where the pin is missing. Say what nil actually means\nand what the portal does with it.\n\nRegenerated CRDs and kcp schemas carry the same text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(kuery): treat the host fetch as sufficient auth\n\nuseKueryApi gated API creation on request.token, but this PR moves providers\nonto the host-owned farosContext.fetch, which injects Authorization itself\nand deprecates the raw token. Once hosts stop exposing the token, Kuery would\nhave sat in \"waiting for workspace context\" forever while being perfectly\nable to make authenticated requests.\n\nExpose hasHostFetch on the request context — true when the host supplied its\nown transport rather than the portalkit token fallback — and accept it as\nauthentication on its own. The token gate now applies only to older hosts\nthat expose no fetch, so both sides of the deprecation window work.\n\nThe test loads the real kuery.ts module graph through vite rather than\ntranspiling one file, keeping Vue external so the module and the test share\none Vue instance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(hub): state pinUIIntegrity''s concurrency contract\n\nThe function doc described the error path''s keep/delete rule for a single\nreconcile only, which read as unconditional. Record that the call is safe\nunder concurrent reconciles for one provider and that the decision is made on\nthe re-read entry, so the next reader of this code does not reintroduce the\nsnapshot-based delete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(portal): apply provider fetch policy after the caller''s init\n\nBoth provider fetch wrappers built their RequestInit as\n{ credentials: ''same-origin'', ...init, headers }. Later keys win in a\nspread, so a caller passing init.credentials overrode the value the\nwrapper exists to enforce. The host wrapper (createProviderFetch) and\nthe portalkit token fallback (providerFetch in tenant.ts) now spread\ninit first and set credentials and headers after it; those are the only\nfields either wrapper owns as policy, and request-shaping fields such as\nmethod, body, mode, redirect and signal remain the caller''s.\n\nThe allow list already confines requests to same-origin paths, where\n''include'' and ''same-origin'' behave the same and ''omit'' only drops\ncookies the bearer auth does not rely on, so this is the boundary\nhonouring its own contract rather than closing a demonstrated bypass.\n\ntenant.ts is the canonical portalkit source; the vendored copies are\nregenerated with make sync-portalkit. Two tests cover both wrappers and\nfail against the previous spread order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(providers): stop claiming the loader sets crossorigin\n\nThree passages still said the bundle loader sets crossorigin=\"anonymous\"\nalongside the SRI hash. providerScriptLoader.ts deliberately sets no\ncrossorigin attribute: the bundle is a same-origin load, for which the\nbrowser enforces integrity without one, and the attribute would turn the\nload into a CORS-mode request that the hub''s UI proxy does not\nnegotiate. The docs now describe the implemented behaviour and the\nreason, so the attribute is not reintroduced from the text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(code-portal): keep the providerFetch import with the other imports\n\nThe static import had landed after the module''s const declarations,\nsplitting the import block. ESM hoists it, so nothing behaved differently,\nbut it read as though the import were order-dependent and it is the kind\nof thing an import-order lint rejects. Moved up beside the type import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"754e4909413ffcf738968c87719e456dc0d2addf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/trees/754e4909413ffcf738968c87719e456dc0d2addf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/commits/acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qaztoAKGFjZGJjNGNjYjUwMTA2YjY0OWQ4MjcxMDAzNGVhODRjN2YwMTU1NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77","sha":"cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77"}],"sha":"acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/acdbc4ccb50106b649d82710034ea84c7f015542"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:03:39Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:03:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(provider-sdk): share one hub heartbeat client across providers (#632)\n\n* refactor(provider-sdk): share one hub heartbeat client across providers\n\nEight providers each carried their own copy of the hub heartbeat loop:\nedges, agents, code, infrastructure and app-studio in a heartbeat.go,\nkuery, quickstart and databricks inline in main.go. Every copy had its\nown FAROS_HUB_INSECURE TLS-skip gate, its own token handling and its own\nfailure logging, so #627 had to change all eight to authenticate the beat\nas the provider service account, and any future change to the heartbeat\n(mutual TLS, backoff, a new hub failure mode) would again land eight\ntimes and could drift between copies.\n\nMove the loop into provider-sdk/hubclient: HeartbeatConfig,\nConfigFromEnv (same env names plus the #627 token fallback) and\nRunHeartbeat, which logs a 401/403 from the hub with an actionable\nmessage now that enforce mode can reject beats. The old behaviour is\nkept as config fields with the previous defaults (immediate first beat,\n30s interval, 5s timeout, exact \"true\" insecure gate, readiness gate for\napp-studio and databricks via CanSend, logr logger for edges). Each\nprovider''s main.go now only builds the config and starts the loop; the\nper-provider heartbeat files are deleted.\n\nAlso trims the trailing newline clientcmd keeps when it reads a\ntokenFile into BearerToken, which left TestTokenFromKubeconfigReadsTokenFile\nred on the #627 branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(provider-sdk): resolve the hub token only when heartbeats are enabled\n\nThree follow-ups on the shared heartbeat client, now that it is the single\nplace deciding heartbeat behaviour for all eight providers.\n\nConfigFromEnv resolved the bearer before anyone could see that the heartbeat\nis disabled. The empty-HubURL check lives in RunHeartbeat, but every call\nsite logs ConfigFromEnv''s error first, so a provider with no FAROS_HUB_URL\ndid a pointless provider-kubeconfig read and logged a confusing token error\nin tests and local runs. #627 fixed exactly this in the eight per-provider\ncopies and replacing them with the shared client undid it. Return early\ninstead; the config stays usable, so RunHeartbeat still takes its existing\ndisabled path and logs its existing line.\n\nTokenFromKubeconfig''s BearerTokenFile fallback is dead code. clientcmd\npopulates rest.Config.BearerToken from either the inline `token` or, when\nonly `tokenFile` is set, that file''s bytes -- both verbatim (client-go\nv0.36.2 tools/clientcmd/client_config.go:277-287), which is what the trim is\nfor. The fallback can therefore only run on a whitespace-only token, where\nre-reading the same file yields the same nothing. Worse, clientcmd uses\n`else if`: when both `token` and `tokenFile` are set the inline token wins\nand the file is deliberately ignored -- and the fallback would have read\nthat ignored file. Delete it and say plainly in the comment what clientcmd\ndoes.\n\nTest the two behaviours the shared client now owns for everyone. A disabled\nheartbeat must not touch the kubeconfig, asserted by pointing\nFAROS_PROVIDER_KUBECONFIG at a directory that errors if read. And a\nFAROS_HUB_URL ending in \"/\" must still POST a clean path: seven of the eight\nproviders concatenated without trimming, so a trailing slash produced a\ndouble slash, gorilla mux cleaned the path and 301''d, Go''s client turned the\nredirected POST into a GET, and the hub answered 405 -- a silent heartbeat\nfailure that made the provider go stale. This branch is what fixes that, so\npin it end to end from the env var to the request line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(providers): drop build references to the deleted heartbeat.go files\n\nReplacing the five per-provider heartbeat.go copies with the shared client\nleft three places still naming them. providers/agents/Dockerfile COPYs its\nsource files by name, so the image build failed outright with\n\"/providers/agents/heartbeat.go\": not found. The Tiltfile listed each\ndeleted file as a live_update/serve dependency for code, app-studio, agents,\ninfrastructure and edges, and the agents architecture doc''s repository\nskeleton still showed the file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ef3aa2af4a967db49ab8dc40c9a19826c4d81bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/trees/2ef3aa2af4a967db49ab8dc40c9a19826c4d81bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/commits/cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qaztoAKGNjOTg2ZWY3ZTRkZjQ3MDU0OGY2YTU1MmZjZTY4MzE2NWE3MmVjNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290","sha":"b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290"}],"sha":"cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/cc986ef7e4df470548f6a552fce683165a72ec77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T08:31:54Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T08:31:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(hub): authenticate provider heartbeats with the provider service account (#627)\n\n* fix(hub): authenticate provider heartbeats with the provider service account\n\nPOST /api/providers/{name}/heartbeat was registered on the root router\nwith no auth middleware in front of it, and the handler never read the\nAuthorization header. Anyone able to reach the hub could keep a dead\nprovider Ready (Provider.Ready() is !HeartbeatStale) and forge its\nreportedVersion, and because the recorder patches CatalogEntry.status the\nfake liveness fanned out to every replica. The handler''s comment claimed\nauth was enforced upstream; nothing upstream did so.\n\nThe handler now takes a HeartbeatAuthenticator. The TokenReview-backed\nimplementation resolves the provider''s workspace cluster, reviews the\nbearer there and requires it to authenticate as\nsystem:serviceaccount:default:provider - the account the hub minted the\nprovider kubeconfig for. Successful verifications are cached for\nHeartbeatTTL/2 keyed by sha256(token)+provider. The review requests no\naudience: the provider kubeconfig token is a legacy\nkubernetes.io/service-account-token Secret token with no aud claim, so a\nworkload-identity audience would reject it. Scoping comes from reviewing\nin the provider''s own logical cluster.\n\n--provider-heartbeat-auth=warn|enforce controls the outcome of a failed\ncheck; warn (log at V(0) with provider and reason, still record) is this\nrelease''s default and the next release flips it to enforce.\n\nProvider side, provider-sdk/hubclient.ResolveHubToken() returns\nFAROS_HUB_TOKEN if set and otherwise the bearer from\nFAROS_PROVIDER_KUBECONFIG; all eight heartbeat clients call it, so charts\nneed no change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(provider-sdk): trim the kubeconfig tokenFile bearer\n\nclientcmd copies a tokenFile into rest.Config.BearerToken verbatim, so a\nhand-written token file''s trailing newline ended up in the Authorization\nheader and TestTokenFromKubeconfigReadsTokenFile failed. Trim it, the\nsame way the inline-token path already does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hub): stop the heartbeat endpoint describing itself to anonymous callers\n\nThe heartbeat endpoint is mounted with no auth middleware in front of it, so\nin enforce mode it was answering unauthenticated callers with the\nauthenticator''s own error text. Those messages are written for the log: they\nname the logical cluster the TokenReview was issued in, the service account\nusername the beat was expected to authenticate as, and whether a CatalogEntry\ncluster is known for the provider at all.\n\nA rejection now carries one short string per status class and nothing that\nvaries with the hub''s state; the full reason stays in the existing log lines,\nwhich is where an operator debugs a provider that cannot beat.\n\nThe registry lookup also moves ahead of the authenticator. Verifying a beat\nfor a name the hub has never heard of cost a TokenReview round trip against\nkcp and, in warn mode, a log line per beat, all driven by an anonymous\ncaller. Returning a bare 404 there would have kept an enumeration oracle\n(today an unknown name draws 503 from the authenticator, which cannot resolve\na cluster for it, while a known name with a bad token draws 401), so enforce\nmode answers an unregistered name with exactly the generic 401 a bad\ncredential gets. Warn mode accepts unauthenticated beats by design, so known\nand unknown are observable there whatever the status is; it keeps the 404.\n\nreg.Get and CatalogEntryCluster are different lookups and disagree during\nstartup: a provider registered before its CatalogEntry has been observed is\nknown to the former and unresolvable by the latter. Only a name absent from\nthe registry short-circuits, so that transient state stays the 503 the\nprovider retries rather than becoming a permanent 401.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(providers): resolve the hub token only when heartbeats are enabled\n\nEvery provider''s runHeartbeat read the provider kubeconfig through\nhubclient.ResolveHubToken before checking whether FAROS_HUB_URL was set, so a\nrun with heartbeats disabled — tests, local invocations — did the kubeconfig\nread for a beat that would never be sent and logged a token error that reads\nlike a real failure.\n\nThe resolution moves below the empty-hub early return in all eight call\nsites; nothing else about the loop changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(providers): scope the heartbeat contract to platform providers\n\nThe heartbeat section and the \"minimal provider backend contract\" both stated\nthe requirement unconditionally, but Registry.Heartbeat is keyed by bare name\nand resolves only platform providers; its own doc comment says an org-owned\nprovider \"cannot beat here\". A BYO provider author following the contract\nwould have implemented a heartbeat that never marks the provider Ready.\n\nSince this branch makes enforce mode answer an unregistered name with the same\ngeneric 401 as a bad credential, that dead end now looks like a credential\nproblem, so say plainly which providers the endpoint serves and where an\norg-owned provider''s readiness comes from instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hub): keep warn-mode heartbeat logs to failures worth acting on\n\nWarn mode logged every failed beat at V(0), including the \"cannot verify\"\nclass. A hub started without kcp answers every provider that way on every\ntick, so the log fills with a line that says nothing about any provider and\nrepeats forever.\n\nSplit by class instead. A rejected or missing identity stays at V(0): that is\nthe list of providers an operator has to fix before enforce becomes the\ndefault, and it is per-provider and actionable. Verification failures drop to\nV(1), because both ways they happen are already reported elsewhere — a hub\nwith no kcp logs that once at startup, and a hub whose kcp is unreachable\nfails the heartbeat recorder, which logs at error level.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"72b448ae43c8ea3e4d6203b3dbfdfcc25a8535d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/trees/72b448ae43c8ea3e4d6203b3dbfdfcc25a8535d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/commits/b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qaztoAKGI1MjRlNjMwNzllMWEyYjcyNTY3MjEzNzZhYzVlMmVmYjY0ZmMyOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f","sha":"486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f"}],"sha":"b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/b524e63079e1a2b7256721376ac5e2efb64fc290"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:37:43Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:37:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: run tests, vet and govulncheck for every Go module (#624)\n\n* ci: run tests, vet and govulncheck for every Go module\n\nThe repo is ten Go modules (root, provider-sdk, eight standalone\nproviders) but CI only ran `make test` on the root module plus a single\npackage of providers/infrastructure, so 8 of 9 non-root modules had no\ntest gate at all. The security fixes queued in\ndocs/security-remediation-plan.md land in providers/edges,\nproviders/agents and pkg/agent; without a gate a fix there can regress\nsilently.\n\nReplace the `test` job with a `test-modules` matrix that runs `go vet`\nand `go test -count=1` (with -race everywhere except providers/edges,\nwhose TestSSHSessionTeardown has a pre-existing test-only race) per\nmodule, and add a non-blocking `govulncheck` matrix that flips to\nblocking once the initial findings are triaged. No go.work is needed:\nevery provider go.mod still replaces provider-sdk to ../../provider-sdk.\nProviders `//go:embed all:portal/dist`, so the jobs stub that directory\nwith a dotfile rather than build every portal a second time.\n\nAdd .github/CODEOWNERS so pull requests touching the hub, agent, server,\nSDK, edges provider, CI/install plumbing, or any auth/proxy/token file\nrequest review from the maintainers. It binds once branch protection\nrequires code-owner review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: bump Go to 1.26.8 and upgrade vulnerable dependencies\n\nThe govulncheck matrix added in the previous commit reported findings for\nall ten modules. Most of them were stdlib: the tree pinned go 1.26.3, and\n1.26.8 is the current patch in that line.\n\nRaise the `go` directive rather than adding a `toolchain` line. Both would\nwork for actions/setup-go, which prefers `toolchain` when it is present, but\nit only consults `toolchain` while GOTOOLCHAIN is not `local` - and a\n`toolchain` line is ignored outright by a local build pinned that way, which\nwould silently reintroduce every stdlib finding. The `go` directive is a hard\nfloor everywhere: setup-go always honours it, and `go build` refuses to\nproceed on an older toolchain instead of quietly using it. Every workflow in\nthe repo resolves its Go version from go.mod, so this covers CI, e2e and\ngoreleaser at once.\n\nThen take every dependency upgrade with an upstream fix, per module and only\nwhere the dependency is actually linked:\n\n  golang.org/x/crypto                v0.54.0 -> v0.56.0   GO-2026-6355/6354/6303\n  go.etcd.io/etcd/{server,client}/v3 v3.6.8  -> v3.6.14   GO-2026-6114/6107/5736\n  google.golang.org/grpc             v1.8x   -> v1.82.1   GO-2026-6061\n  oras.land/oras-go/v2               v2.6.0  -> v2.6.1    GO-2026-5885/5884\n  github.com/containerd/containerd   v1.7.30 -> v1.7.33   GO-2026-5758/5475/5378\n  go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlpmetric/otlpmetrichttp\n                                     v1.40.0 -> v1.43.0   GO-2026-4985 (edges)\n  github.com/jackc/pgx/v5            v5.6.0  -> v5.9.2    GO-2026-5004 (kuery)\n\nThe last two were not in the original triage; they only became visible once\nthe noise ahead of them cleared. GO-2026-5004 is the one that mattered: a SQL\ninjection via placeholder confusion, reachable from the kuery query API''s\nServeHTTP, not a transitive init-only path.\n\nThe etcd and grpc bumps were the risky ones - etcd comes in through the\nembedded kcp server - but every module builds, vets and race-tests clean, so\nnothing had to be reverted. `go mod tidy` also dropped a handful of stale\nrequirements that were already unused.\n\nWhat is left after this is six advisories with no upstream fix; the next\ncommit handles those.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: make govulncheck blocking with an explicit allowlist\n\nThe govulncheck matrix was continue-on-error \"until the initial findings are\ntriaged\". They are triaged now, so drop it - a permanently red check that\ncannot fail is worse than no check, because nobody reads it.\n\n`govulncheck ./...` cannot be the gate on its own. It exits 3 whether a\nvulnerability is reachable or merely sits in the module graph, and it has no\nsuppression mechanism at all, so a single advisory with no upstream fix pins\nthe job red forever. Two small pieces fix that:\n\n  hack/govulncheck/main.go   reads the JSON stream (concatenated objects, not\n                             NDJSON, so it needs a streaming decoder) and\n                             reports a finding only when trace[0] names a\n                             function - i.e. govulncheck reached the symbol,\n                             not just the module. Drops allowlisted IDs and\n                             exits 1 on anything left, printing the module,\n                             the fixed version and the go get line.\n\n  hack/govulncheck-allow.yaml  the accepted residue. Every entry needs an id,\n                             the module it comes from, why it cannot be fixed,\n                             why the exposure is acceptable here, and a\n                             review-by date. Six entries today, all with no\n                             upstream fix: x/crypto/openpgp (deprecated, and\n                             pinned by helm''s provenance code), two Moby\n                             daemon-side defects reached through the docker\n                             client that `faros dev plugin` uses, and three\n                             containerd CRI checkpoint/restore defects reached\n                             through helm''s OCI registry client. In every case\n                             the only traced frames are package init\n                             functions; faros runs neither daemon.\n\nA stale entry - an allowlisted ID whose module is still linked but which no\nlonger reports anything - warns and does not fail. Failing there would mean\nthe gate punishes whoever lands the upgrade that fixed it. Same for a passed\nreview-by date.\n\nhack/govulncheck.sh drives both over one or more modules, stubs portal/dist\nfor the go:embed and cleans up after itself, so the workflow step is one line\nand the same command works locally: `make govulncheck`.\n\nAll ten modules pass the gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"37dc25707718026ed66fa597c5b16e7d5af60921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/trees/37dc25707718026ed66fa597c5b16e7d5af60921"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/git/commits/486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f","node_id":"C_kwDOS3qaztoAKDQ4NmExYTg1ZWFlOTcxM2QwMGNhOTI3MGUzNjk5NWQ0OTEyOWE0NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/provider-code/commit/fb5d1d78bd25eaa3d69503cf4f99240bfe93be73","sha":"fb5d1d78bd25eaa3d69503cf4f99240bfe93be73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/fb5d1d78bd25eaa3d69503cf4f99240bfe93be73"}],"sha":"486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/provider-code/commits/486a1a85eae9713d00ca9270e36995d49129a45f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5685031?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cwilhit","id":5685031,"login":"cwilhit","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODUwMzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwilhit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/